{"tool_name":"ccp4mg","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"ccp4mg","home":"http://www.ccp4.ac.uk/MG/","summary":"CCP4 Molecular graphics package Topic: Crystallography.","addition_date":"2015-03-26T21:55:52Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:10:06.246715Z","tool_type":["Desktop application"],"version":["2.8.1"],"collections":["Instruct"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:ccp4mg","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"ccisb@stfc.ac.uk","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"Instruct","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.ccp4.ac.uk/MG/ccp4mg_help/index.html"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://www.ccp4.ac.uk/MG/ccp4mg_help/tutorial/index.html"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["mwinn"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0883"},"format":[{"term":"PDB","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1476"}]}],"note":"CCP4 Molecular graphics package","operation":[{"term":"Structure visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0570"}]}],"name":"CCP4mg","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Instruct","publication":[{"doi":"10.1107/s0907444911007281","metadata":{"abstract":"CCP4mg is a molecular-graphics program that is designed to give rapid access to both straightforward and complex static and dynamic representations of macromolecular structures. It has recently been updated with a new interface that provides more sophisticated atom-selection options and a wizard to facilitate the generation of complex scenes. These scenes may contain a mixture of coordinate-derived and abstract graphical objects, including text objects, arbitrary vectors, geometric objects and imported images, which can enhance a picture and eliminate the need for subsequent editing. Scene descriptions can be saved to file and transferred to other molecules. Here, the substantially enhan